stream
BT
/F1 20.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 742.00 Tm (Chapter 5 Distributed Transactions) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 728.00 Tm (Cross service operations need atomicity rebuilt above the database boundary.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 714.00 Tm (Network timeouts make it impossible to distinguish a failed commit from a lost response.) Tj
/F1 14.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 694.40 Tm (5.1 Two-Phase Commit) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 680.40 Tm (A coordinator asks participants to vote, then decides commit or abort.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 666.40 Tm (The coordinator is a single point of failure and participants block while holding locks.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 652.40 Tm (A participant that voted yes cannot decide on its own: it must wait for the coordinator decision.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 638.40 Tm (Presumed abort and presumed commit recovery protocols reduce the blocking window at the cost of extra rules.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
