8 0 obj
<< /Length 675 >>
stream
BT
/F1 14.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 750.40 Tm (5.3 Saga) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 736.40 Tm (Saga runs local transactions and compensates them in reverse order on failure.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 722.40 Tm (It does not provide isolation, so intermediate states are visible to readers.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 708.40 Tm (Compensations must be idempotent because a retry can execute the same step twice.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 694.40 Tm (Orchestration keeps the workflow in one service, while choreography distributes it across events.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 680.40 Tm (Saga suits order fulfilment and travel booking, where intermediate states are acceptable.) Tj
ET
endstream
